{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Source verification (2026-08-09): the ticket's original hypothesis that the intended source was rebar epic 3006-e198-13db-4e1f is DISPROVED. 3006 was created 2026-07-03 — a month after these citations arrived in this repository with the DSO extraction commit b534f47a7f (2026-06-08) and six weeks after the 2026-05-24 ACLI audit they describe — and its plan never mentions ACLI. The verified source is the pre-extraction DSO epic 3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f (closed, 24 children, 'level-triggered reconciler'), recorded in the DSO ticket-data mining report on the tickets branch under 63cc-ec94-4792-464b; it is the only DSO-era id beginning 3a03 anywhere in this repository's history, and the same file cites its sibling DSO bug ids (c916-74a1-ed06-40e4, 4fa9-0846-519e-4c30, 5010-1c6a-9387-4b5b) in full form. All three citations now spell the full id and label it pre-extraction DSO. Gerrit change 1572."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786309764096210001,"uuid":"287ff6ef-fe52-483e-8856-6d9bff283b64"}